{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1524512-wound-penalty-application","id":1524512,"title":"Wound Penalty application","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-25T16:39:28-07:00","id":1524512,"title":"Wound Penalty application","content":"We use penalty dice since the beggining but as st i've always felt that they were way less effective on powerful character. An old vampire, pc or npc, with potence or celerity could have up to 15 dice to roll maybe more if low generation, and the biggest wound penalty is -5 dice wich mean that vampire could get from 15 to 10 or 17 to 12 and so on, which is still a lot for a character that is supposed to be so badly wounded that he can only crawl on the ground<br /> <br /> Don't you think a difficulty penalty would be more effective? A +1 diff for hurt and injured health level, +2 diff for wounded and mauled and +3 for crippled seems appropriate especially about the higher botch risk and would fit for any pool may they be weak, average or powerfull, no? What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T03:47:48-07:00","id":1524518,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would be that effective of a house rule. If you make wounds bad enough that the highest end characters are really hampered by them, then more average characters are going to get hosed instead.<br /> <br /> Higher difficult has less impact the more dice you have. The &quot;increased botch&quot; risk is not what people tend to think of it. Once you get past 8 dice, the odds of botching constantly go down regardless of difficulty. What happens, is that the percentage of non-successful rolls becomes more botch loaded even as the odds of non-succeeding decrease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T05:28:56-07:00","id":1524522,"title":"","content":"Then is there a better way to impact powerfull characters? Of course when a charcter is crippled he can only move up to 1m per turn and cannot move and take an action at the same time but RAW tell that if that crippled charcter choose to take an action, let's say dodge or block he will have diff 5 and 5dice penalty while he can only crawl on the ground due to pain and his physical condition. A crippled low gen vampire with 15 dice will be able to dodge with 10 dice diff 5 for a brawl attack, the penalty is not as effective as it would be.<br /> <br /> Playing with difficulty penalty would reduce their success enough to make them weaker, the purpose is not to make them fail but a badly injured character is supposed to be less and less effective as his wound become more serious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T11:35:47-07:00","id":1524535,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you can really do anything simple that would make wound penalties that scale better without a massive overhaul of the base systems.<br /> <br /> While it would be a bit annoying in terms of in-play math, the &quot;middle ground&quot; option I can think of would be to make wound penalties into fraction multipliers. Something like -1 being multiply your dice pool by 3/4, than 1/2, than 1/4. This would mean a character with 8 dice would lose 2 dice, 4 dice, and than 6 dice, while a character with 16 dice would lose -4, -8, and finally -12.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:17:31-07:00","id":1524538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1524512-wound-penalty-application?p=1524535#post1524535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you can really do anything simple that would make wound penalties that scale better without a massive overhaul of the base systems.<br /> <br /> While it would be a bit annoying in terms of in-play math, the &quot;middle ground&quot; option I can think of would be to make wound penalties into fraction multipliers. Something like -1 being multiply your dice pool by 3/4, than 1/2, than 1/4. This would mean a character with 8 dice would lose 2 dice, 4 dice, and than 6 dice, while a character with 16 dice would lose -4, -8, and finally -12.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not that good in math unfortunatly 'x)<br /> And if we limit the dice pool to a max depending on the wounds? When you drive the w20 rule p.275 and 276 say your vehicule define how many dice you can roll depending on it's manoeuvrability, adapt this to the penalty coudl eventually work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T13:49:19-07:00","id":1524548,"title":"","content":"While that would limit huge dice-pools without inherently screwing more average characters, there's a bunch of weird knock on effects (nerfing autofire with guns), and you have to figure out caps that don''t let average characters off the hook either. A character that's taken 6 HL of damage shouldn't be facing no penalties because their base dice-pools are already below the cap anyway.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that you're going to run the risk of this turning into an attrition war instead of really making fights more fun/interesting. Older and more powerful vampires means more blood to heal damage to get out of nasty wound levels, and more Willpower to spend to ignore wound penalties for a turn. If you use wounds to &quot;even&quot; the playing field too much, you run the risk of making it even more likely the PCs die in serious fights. While powerful characters can take a massive dice penalty in stride and still throw big attacks, it also means they're just as capable of retreating if a fight isn't going their way. Older vampires are more incline to retreat and continue to exist than fight to the final death because the enemy could always get lucky even if the odds are on your side. The harder you make retreating, the more powerful combat elders are going to opt for killing anyone attacking them as quickly as possible instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T13:31:21-07:00","id":1524603,"title":"","content":"In the case of old vampire they would certainly retreat, but when you think of a massive thunderwyrm, powerful fomori or elder bsd it's less certain.<br /> Even if it's lore the story that made me think that actual wound penalty are not effective enough is the story of mithras, from what i've read after a fight against a pack of garou he was so wounded that a fledgling manage to finish him. It's the lore It's not supposed to be analized through the game rule (and we don't know what gift has been used on him), but still i can't help but think that a vampire that old and powerfull could've been killed with a -2 or even a -5 dice when a read his character sheet is not realistic (link from my source: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mithras_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mithras_(VTM</a>) ).<br /> That's why i think the wound penalty should be revised","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T14:14:11-07:00","id":1524605,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to say that wound penalties as written are great... I'm just saying that revising them in a fashion that will improve things over all is going to be very difficult without making much bigger changes to the system. There's only so many variables to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T11:15:45-07:00","id":1524648,"title":"","content":"We can still throw ideas and see if they can be adapted. The difficulty penalty is simple but has it's bad side for average character, capping pool can work if we adapt the shooting mechanic and low pool, increase the dice penalty with pool higher than 10 would require math to make it balanced...<br /> <br /> I'm sure something can be done","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}